From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0250: Goodix probe: QSEE log, the TA's real name, power timings

0249 reached PRE_DETECT and got GF_ERROR_CHIP_ID_NOT_CORRECT (1043). To see
what the TA read, the QSEE log buffer (TZ_OS_REGISTER_LOG_BUFFER, 32 KB in the
pool) is registered once before APP_START and its new lines are logged as
"TZ <cmd>|..." after APP_START, APP_SHUTDOWN and every command (bounded ring
reads, v1/v2 header detected). TZ knows the app as "fingerprint" (goodixfp.b03
metadata), so lookup and shutdown use that name and op 1 really restarts it.
Power-up waits 20 ms after gpio65 before the reset pulse; gpio104 is otherwise
pulsed only after WAKEUP(reset), not on FAILED_AND_RETRY. Op 6 = op 1 with
slow timings (100 ms settle, 120 ms after each reset); op 7 reads L9's PMIC
registers back over the SPMI observer (read only).
